From 370edb6ee62787f61f193edb1d0db97253fd07b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:23:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Thread the software renderers (nuubOS)

On the H700 (4x Cortex-A53) the emulation thread was also drawing both
2D engines (~10 ms a frame in Mario Kart DS) and a single render thread
needed ~23 ms for the 3D picture.

- 3D: the threaded soft renderer splits the screen in two halves, lines
  [0, 96) on the render thread and [96, 192) on a second one (per-lane
  polygon edge state; a lane starts by placing the edges at its first
  line, which Slope::Setup computes exactly like stepping). The final
  pass of the boundary lines waits for the raw neighbour line of the
  other half; each half releases its lines to GetLine in order.
- 3D color buffer double-buffered: the next frame renders into the other
  buffer, so the 2D engines may still read this frame's lines during
  VBlank. Frame start selects the buffer and whether GetLine must wait.
  GetLine waits on a per-buffer, per-line ready flag set after the final
  pass (cleared when a render into that buffer starts): the upstream
  line-count semaphore drifted whenever a rendered frame was not drawn by
  the 2D engines, and then handed out lines still being rendered.
- 2D: with the threaded renderer the 2D engines draw on a worker thread.
  A job covers a run of scanlines (up to 16) over which nothing the
  worker reads changed: a copy of a unit is sent only when its register
  generation (Unit::RegGen, bumped by every emulation-side change)
  moved, palette and OAM only when written; VCount runs along. VRAM flattening stays on the
  emulation thread. Fields the renderer advances per line (affine
  reference points, mosaic counters, the horizontal window flags) stay the
  worker's unless the
  emulation side set them (per-field generation counters). Frames with a
  display capture are drawn on the emulation thread as before. Drained
  before the framebuffers flip, on savestates and resets.

Upstream: not submitted (nuubOS H700 performance work).
